{"id": "unknown-2026-09-24-005", "date": "2026-09-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak", "uncertainty"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "North India cotton yarn steady amid weak demand, cautious buying", "content": "Cotton yarn stayed steady but bearish in Ludhiana and Delhi as payment constraints, weak demand and cautious weaving buying capped trade.\nPanipat recycled yarn saw limited buying, with festival stocks and home-textile export uncertainty weighing on sentiment.\nCotton prices held steady as smaller mills bought spot needs, while larger mills stayed away amid sufficient stocks and new arrivals.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/north-india-cotton-yarn-steady-amid-weak-demand-cautious-buying-313752-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-24-006", "date": "2026-09-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Slight change in ICE cotton futures as traders await demand signal", "content": "ICE December 2026 cotton settled two points higher at 82.89 cents per pound after trading between 82.18 and 83.48 cents.\nVolume fell to 35,528 contracts from 52,195, suggesting traders are holding back from large positions after two volatile sessions.\nExport demand remains weak, China’s direct buying is limited, and US harvest progress, yields and cotton quality remain key supply factors.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/slight-change-in-ice-cotton-futures-as-traders-await-demand-signal-313744-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-24-007", "date": "2026-09-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh introduces Taka settlement framework for cross-border trade", "content": "Bangladesh Bank has opened a Taka settlement route for eligible cross-border trade through Non-Resident Taka vostro accounts at authorised dealer banks.\nLetters of credit and contracts will stay in admissible currencies, with invoice values converted into Taka at prevailing rates.\nEligible exporters retain foreign currency facilities for input imports and Export Development Fund loan repayment.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-introduces-taka-settlement-framework-for-cross-border-trade-313733-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "nike-2026-09-24-008", "date": "2026-09-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": ["nike", "adidas"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.7, "reasons": ["多公司提及"]}, "title": "Can On’s running technology find a place in football?", "content": "On has named football and golf as growth categories through 2029, alongside running, sneaker and apparel businesses, and is targeting net sales of at least CHF 5.6 billion.\nFootball boots are reportedly due only in 2027, as the Swiss sportswear brand enters a category long controlled by Nike, Adidas and Puma.\nOn is betting on LightSpray, Kylian Mbappé and Thierry Henry to drive adoption.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/can-on-s-running-technology-find-a-place-in-football--313743-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-24-009", "date": "2026-09-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India seeks to strengthen physical & digital export support: Goyal", "content": "India plans to train about 1,000 local personnel in regional languages to help existing and prospective exporters at district and state levels.\nTextile, man-made fibre and other sectors raised issues on FTA use, documentation, logistics, standards and testing.\nA Trade Connect platform is being developed to give product- and HSN-wise tariff, FTA and procedure information.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-seeks-to-strengthen-physical-digital-export-support-goyal-313727-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-24-010", "date": "2026-09-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Global supply shifts open growth window for Indian apparel: Report", "content": "India held about 3 per cent of global apparel exports in 2025, while China’s share fell to 27.3 per cent from 36.9 per cent in 2010, PL Capital said.\nBangladesh and Vietnam have captured more of the shift, lifting their combined share to over 13 per cent.\nTrade access, China+1 sourcing and policy support could favour large, integrated Indian garment exporters.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/global-supply-shifts-open-growth-window-for-indian-apparel-report-313713-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-24-011", "date": "2026-09-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "China gains as Bangladesh loses share in Denmark apparel market", "content": "Denmark’s apparel imports fell 4.9 per cent to $2.595 billion in January–June 2026 from $2.728 billion a year earlier.\nChina’s shipments rose 5.4 per cent to $568.519 million, lifting its share to 21.91 per cent; Bangladesh fell 13.1 per cent to $438.509 million.\nGermany stayed third, Sweden moved close behind and Poland ranked fifth as the top five suppliers held 62.81 per cent of imports.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/china-gains-as-bangladesh-loses-share-in-denmark-apparel-market-313679-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
